When using Lavaan package in R software, I have a question about how to display more decimal places for model fit indices (i.e., CFI, RMSEA, SRMR). Typically, Lavaan displays results of 3 decimal places for fit indices. Are there any ways I could allow Lavaan to display more than 3 decimal places?

I have checked in the group and found a related post: Display more digits after decimal point (google.com) <https://groups.google.com/g/lavaan/c/VdF0KsLyrdE/m/sO088u2o1FoJ>. However, when I try the codes in the post, I still could not allow Lavaan to display more than 3 decimal places for model fit indices. Are there any ways to solve this issue?

Thank you very much for your help in advance!

Yours sincerely,
Benjamin Wang

