Hi,

You cannot because the model is not identified.

You have 6 covariances in the data and you are trying to estimate 3 exogenous covariances and 6 paths. You cannot estimate 9 things from 6 things. The model would be specified as follows, but you will just get an error that the model is not identified:

library(lavaan)

# Generate correlated variables

N <- 1000

X <- rnorm(N)

d <- data.frame(A=X+rnorm(N),

                B=X+rnorm(N),

                C=X+rnorm(N),

                E=X+rnorm(N))

sem('

#Regression Model

D ~ A+B+C

D =~ E

E~ A+C

', data = d)

Mikko

