Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Hello

I am wondering what assumption lavaan does about the distribution of the latent factors when estimating them.

Does it assume joint normality or a mixture of normal distribution of the two factors?

In order to be more concrete, let me please provide you with this example:

model <- '
# 1st factor
#loadings
F1=~    1*x1 +  x2 +   x3
# threshold
x1          | 0*t1 + t2
x2          | t1 + t2
x3          | t1 + t2
# mean and std of factor
F1   ~~ NA* F1
F1  ~ NA*1

#2nd factor
#loadings
F2=~    1*x4 +  x5 +   x6
# threshold
x4          | 0*t1 + t2
x5          | t1 + t2
x6          | t1 + t2
# mean and std of factor
F2   ~~ NA* F2
F2  ~ NA*1
'
sem <- sem(model , data=my_data, std.lv <http://std.lv>=F, estimator="dwls",parameterization="theta")

Many thanks
Dea

